dict(param='STD', score=3, stance='supports', key='kosminTimeItsAdversaries2018', where='p. 15', quote='the empire’s rulers and subjects inhabited public and private worlds that were comprehensively marked by this new era-time. Three case studies—of fiscality (taxes, archives, and their authorizing procedures), trade (coinage, weights and measures, and the agora), and imperial communications—demonstrate how the Seleucid temporal regime could model administrative procedures and penetrate deep into social life.', note='The Seleucid Era: a continuous imperial count from 311 BCE, used in Babylonian tablets. Only the introduction is in the folder.'),
dict(param='FISC', score=3, stance='supports', key='monerieLeconomieBabylonieLepoque2018', where='p. 238', quote='le témoignage de la documentation cunéiforme y est complété par l’apport de quelque 14 450 timbres fiscaux estampillés sur des bullae et cretulae d’argile mises au jour dans la région, qui portent en général une courte inscription grecque accompagnée d’une date', note='Over 99% from the archive building of Seleucia-on-the-Tigris; taxes in kind, in silver and service (§§ 1.1-1.3). The documents they sealed (on parchment) are lost.'),
dict(param='STD', score=3, stance='supports', key='monerieLeconomieBabylonieLepoque2018', where='p. 276', quote='Le iiie s. séleucide semble donc avoir été marqué par une intégration pleine et entière de la Babylonie à l’espace monétaire séleucide. Celle-ci se caractérisa par l’abandon du système monétaire mixte au profit d’une production unifiée de monnayages royaux d’étalon attique', note='Turning point under Antiochus I (281-261).'),
dict(param='HIER', score=2, stance='qualifies', key='monerieLeconomieBabylonieLepoque2018', where='p. 277', quote='Les Séleucides semblent en effet avoir ménagé une place bien plus importante aux communautés locales, en s’appuyant sur la notabilité liée aux sanctuaires suméro-akkadiens pour l’administration des villes anciennes', note='Crown sustained these local intermediaries by land grants, benefactions and tax exemptions.'),
dict(param='TCTL', score=1, stance='qualifies', key='monerieLeconomieBabylonieLepoque2018', where='p. 277', quote='la Couronne devait assurer la viabilité économique de ces relais locaux par des donations foncières, des actions évergétiques ou des exemptions fiscales', note='Temples as local partners of the crown rather than state units.'),
dict(param='COMM', score=2, stance='supports', key='monerieCompendiumOfficialCorrespondence2023', where='p. 63', quote='it is an Akkadian translation of a collection of Greek official documents issued by the Seleucid administration in the first quarter of the third century BC, concerning the rebuilding of the Bīt Rēš', note='Royal letters reached the Uruk temple authorities in Greek; the Greek parchment originals are lost.'),
dict(param='HIER', score=2, stance='supports', key='monerieCompendiumOfficialCorrespondence2023', where='p. 74', quote='Kidin-Anu also acted as “Elder Brother” (ahu rabû) of the Bīt Rēš, the temple’s most prominent sacerdotal position at the time, which probably explains why he was both the head of the city’s assembly and the main local interlocutor of the Seleucid administration, just like the high administrator (šatammu) of the Esagil temple in Babylon.', note='Local temple elites as the crown’s intermediaries.'),
dict(param='TCTL', score=1, stance='supports', key='monerieCompendiumOfficialCorrespondence2023', where='p. 78', quote='YOS 20, 87 indisputably shows an active support from the Crown, which enabled the Urukean authorities to organize a cultic refoundation in the Bīt Rēš', note='Alexander "revived the old Sumero-Akkadian custom of royal patronage over the temples"; royal patronage rather than state management.'),
dict(param='PRIV', score=2, stance='qualifies', key='coroPrebendeTempliEta2005', where='p. 5', quote='Benché documentino l’attività, nel mercato delle prebende, di individui che richiamano per lo più la propria appartenenza a pochi tra i grandi clan della Uruk del tempo, si tratta di documenti emananti dal tempio e dunque di natura ufficiale piuttosto che privata.', note='Following Beaulieu 1989. Same page describes the tablets: about 1 cm thick, "di forma quadrangolare bombata (circa 10-12 centimetri per lato)", sealed on all four edges. Corpus: 536 archival texts from Seleucid Uruk (Doty).'),
dict(param='PRIV', score=2, stance='supports', key='coroPrebendeTempliEta2005', where='p. 13', quote='L’isqu ha decisamente assunto tutte le caratteristiche della proprietà privata: è soggetta a compravendita e locazione, può costituire corredo dotale e sembra divenire appannaggio di un ceto sociale specifico.', note='Prebends "nelle mani di poche famiglie".'),
dict(param='TERR', score=3, stance='supports', key='kosminLandElephantKings2014', where='pp. 15-16', quote='The Seleucids ruled over a great part of this landscape of “Asia,” depositing their evidentiary trace, for almost two and a half centuries. The diversity and size of the empire and its neighbors and the patchiness of source survival have rendered its political history both byzantine and dispiritingly lacunose.', note='Empire organised in satrapies (Babylonia, Susiane, the "Upper Satrapies").'),
dict(param='SCHOOL', score=1, stance='supports', key='clancierCuneiformCulturesLast2011', where='p. 757', quote='Other families seem, in the same way, to have specialized in particular professions. For example, the descendants of Ekur-zakir were often exorcists and sometimes also astrologers. Many descendants of Ah’utu held administrative responsibilities in the temple and sometimes also the city. There is a strong correlation between specific families and the area of their professional expertise (Doty 1977).', note='Cuneiform learning transmitted in temple-linked families; tablet collections in private houses (p. 755).'),
dict(param='LAW', score=2, stance='supports', key='clancierCuneiformCulturesLast2011', where='pp. 764-765', quote='Civil judicial courts had to be able to use the documents.', note='Leather (alphabetic) originals required before royal courts; cuneiform clay copies valid before the temple court.'),
dict(param='BUR', score=1, stance='supports', key='clancierCuneiformCulturesLast2011', where='p. 764', quote='To conclude, there was a clear hierarchy in the writing media used in Hellenistic Uruk. From a legal perspective, the most important medium was leather, inscribed in alphabetic script, as it was readable and acceptable to the Greek authorities and moreover difficult to corrupt.', note='Cuneiform clay restricted to the temple community; state bureaucracy wrote on leather.'),
dict(param='TEMP', score=3, stance='supports', key='clancierCuneiformCulturesLast2011', where='p. 757', quote='The temples also owned sizeable cattle herds and large parcels of fields around Uruk and in other parts of Babylonia.'),
